 "lines": [
  {
   "start": 0.5,
   "end": 5.749,
   "text": "Six days later, Jesus took Peter, James, and John up a high mountain.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 6.149,
   "end": 14.631,
   "text": "There, in front of them, he was transfigured. His clothes became dazzling white, whiter than anyone on earth could make them.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 15.431,
   "end": 19.315,
   "text": "Then Elijah and Moses appeared, talking with Jesus.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 19.715,
   "end": 26.696,
   "text": "Teacher, it is good for us to be here! Let us put up three shelters: one for you, one for Moses, and one for Elijah.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 27.096,
   "end": 34.125,
   "text": "He did not know what to say, they were so afraid. Then a cloud covered them, and a voice came from the cloud:",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 34.525,
   "end": 37.713,
   "text": "This is my Son, whom I love. Listen to him!",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 38.613,
   "end": 43.596,
   "text": "Suddenly, when they looked around, they saw no one with them, only Jesus.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 44.196,
   "end": 48.066,
   "text": "At the foot of the mountain, a father cried out from the crowd.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 48.366,
   "end": 54.824,
   "text": "Teacher, my son has a spirit that throws him to the ground. Your disciples could not drive it out. If you can do anything, help us!",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 55.224,
   "end": 59.099,
   "text": "If you can? Everything is possible for one who believes.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 59.599,
   "end": 62.151,
   "text": "I do believe! Help me overcome my unbelief!",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 62.851,
   "end": 71.412,
   "text": "Jesus rebuked the spirit. The boy shook, then lay still, like he was dead. But Jesus took him by the hand, and lifted him up.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 72.112,
   "end": 77.373,
   "text": "Later, on the road, the disciples argued about which of them was the greatest.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 77.773,
   "end": 82.83,
   "text": "Anyone who wants to be first must be the very last, and the servant of all.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 83.33,
   "end": 87.469,
   "text": "Then he took a little child, and held the child in his arms.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 87.869,
   "end": 92.501,
   "text": "Whoever welcomes one of these little children in my name, welcomes me.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 93.001,
   "end": 97.815,
   "text": "Even a cup of water given in my name will not lose its reward.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 98.715,
   "end": 102.182,
   "text": "Follow for part fourteen.",
   "tempter": false
  }
 ]
}